# JVM plugin

- Depend on `dynamic-bot-core` public APIs only (same boundary as `dynamic-bot-onebot`). This plugin lives in `com.incubator4.dynamic.koishi`; core types stay `top.colter.dynamic.core.*`.
- Implement `AccountRoutedMessageSinkPlugin`: send, recall, `listMessageSinkRoutes`, `listMessageTargets`.
- `supportedTargetPlatforms` is the live set of `bot.platform` from `bots.list` / `bot.changed`. Include `onebot` (Koishi `adapter-onebot`). Exclude official Koishi `qq` so it does not collide with native `dynamic-bot-onebot`. Do not hardcode Discord/Telegram/KOOK/Lark/OneBot as the only platforms.
- `supportedTargetKinds` is the live union of `target.user` / `target.group` / `target.channel` / `target.thread` from those bots. Match kind against the bots on that platform. Do not hardcode USER/GROUP/CHANNEL/THREAD.
- `routeId` = `koishi:{platform}:{selfId}`. Do not store bot tokens in plugin config (only Gateway URL + token).
- Map `core.Message` → **generated** proto `SendParams`. Do not send raw `Message` JSON to Koishi.
- Map proto `message.created` → `IncomingMessage` + `IncomingMessagePublishRequest`. Build `dedupeKey` / `traceId` on the JVM; do not ask Koishi to classify commands.
- Bot `status`: `READY` = Koishi `ONLINE`; `CONNECTING` = `CONNECT`/`RECONNECT`; `UNAVAILABLE` = `OFFLINE`/`DISCONNECT`. Only `READY` may send.
- Send timeout → `MessageSendResult.uncertain` (`UNKNOWN`), never automatic retry-as-failure.
- Media: pass URIs on DBK. Koishi fetches them before adapter send. Do not copy OneBot local-file / base64 probing unless measured necessary.
- FatJar into dynamic-bot `plugins/`. Do not shade Koishi or Node.
- Do not hardcode the product version. `plugin.yml` and `DBK_APP_VERSION` come from `git describe` (override with `DBK_VERSION`).
